Show a session's exit node in the composer's environment menu.

When the session's repositories name a tailnet exit node, the menu has an
"Exit node" row under Pod, from the runner's report (server patch
0021-environment-exit-node.patch): "cronos-vpn · connected"; in red
"cronos-vpn · offline" with "The session has no internet until it's back.";
in amber "None · the repositories name different ones (a, b)"; in red
"couldn't use it" with Tailscale's error; "not in use" when the Pod doesn't
use it; or just the name when tailscaled didn't answer. Without an exit node
there's no row.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0035.
